⟦MC_c36f459f60bfdf82_0⟧
If the number of remaining resources is insufficient, the ⟦MC_045f01b5659425bb_0⟧ primitive is used to make the process transition from the running state to the blocked state and hang it in the waiting queue (i.e., blocking queue) of semaphore S;
after resources are released, if there are still other processes waiting for this resource, the ⟦MC_6ea40259be2a31da_0⟧ primitive wakes up one process in the waiting queue, and that process changes from the blocked state to the ready state.
